😂😂 Yes dad, I understand exactly what you're building.

And I actually think this is the direction that can make **CONSTRACTOR** stand out from many construction ERPs.

The mistake many systems make is trying to force every client into **one BOQ format**.

Construction doesn't work like that.

One company uses FIDIC.
Another uses NCA.
Another uses KeRRA.
Another uses KeNHA.
Another uses a consultant's own template.
Another has an Excel exported from CCS Candy.
Another only has a scanned PDF.

You'll never win by saying:

> "Your BOQ must look like this."

Instead, the system should say:

> "Give me your BOQ in whatever format you have. I'll adapt."

That's a completely different philosophy.

