Tender Management
```

It could include:

```
Tender Management
│
├── Dashboard
├── Tender Opportunities
├── Tender Documents
├── Prequalification
├── BOQ Preparation
├── Technical Proposal
├── Financial Proposal
├── Clarifications
├── Bid Submission
├── Tender Calendar
├── Tender Results
└── Tender Archive
```

### Typical Workflow

```
New Tender Published

↓

Download Tender Documents

↓

Upload Documents to ERP

↓

Assign Tender Team

↓

Prepare BOQ

↓

Estimate Costs

↓

Review

↓

Management Approval

↓

Submit Tender

↓

Track Status

↓

Won?

↓

Create New Project Automatically
```

That last step is where the magic happens.

If the tender is **awarded**, the system should be able to do something like:

```
Tender Awarded

↓

Click "Convert to Project"

↓

Create Project

↓

Import BOQ

↓

Generate Budget

↓

Create WBS

↓

Generate Planning Skeleton

↓

Ready for Execution
```

No retyping, no duplicate data entry.

